--- body ---
## Context

Tickets with a `Closed:` header (or closed status in log) accumulate in
`tickets/` because there is no binary command to move them to
`tickets/closed/`. Agents and humans do this manually via `git mv`, which
requires knowing the convention and risks moving tickets that are still
blocking others.

`erg archive [id...]` (no args = all) moves closed tickets to `tickets/closed/`
after verifying they are not blocking any open ticket via `Blocked-by`.

## Actions

Implement `erg archive [id...] [dir]`:
1. Collect targets: if IDs given, find those specific ticket files; else scan
   `dir` (default `tickets/`) for tickets with a non-empty `Closed:` header.
2. For each target, check that no open ticket in `dir` has a `Blocked-by`
   pointing to the target's ID. If any do, print a warning and skip that ticket.
3. Move qualifying tickets to `tickets/closed/` via `os.Rename` (same
   filesystem, so atomic).
4. Print `ARCHIVED <filename>` for each moved ticket, `SKIPPED <filename>
   (blocked by <id>)` for each skipped.
5. Exit 0 if at least one ticket was archived or checked; exit 1 on filesystem
   errors.

## Exit criteria

- `erg archive` with no args moves all `Closed:`-headered tickets from
  `tickets/` to `tickets/closed/`.
- A ticket blocked by an open ticket is skipped with a clear warning.
- A ticket with no `Closed:` header is silently ignored.
- `erg archive 0037` archives a specific ticket by ID.
- Test: create two closed tickets (one blocked by an open ticket), run
  `erg archive`, verify only the unblocked one moved.
